            </div>
            <div class="card">
                <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-heart"></i> Remember</h2>
                <ul class="capability-list">
                    <li><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check"></i> You can use SilverAssist whenever you need help.</li>
                    <li><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check"></i> You do not need to complete the guides in order.</li>
                    <li><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check"></i> If you are unsure how to do something: stop and read the instructions again, look at the picture for that step, and follow one step at a time.</li>
                    <li><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check"></i> Use the links on SilverAssist to move to another guide when you need help.</li>
                    <li><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check"></i> Take your time. There is no need to rush.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 7. QUIZ SECTION -->
        <section id="page-quiz" class="page-section">
            <div class="card">
                <button class="btn btn-secondary" onclick="navigateTo('safety')"><i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Stay Safe</button>
                <h1>Avoid Scamming</h1>
                <p>Choose the quiz you want to complete.</p>

                <div class="topic-grid">
                    <div class="card topic-card topic-quiz">
                        <h2><span class="topic-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-shield-halved"></i></span> Lesson 1</h2>
                        <p>Scam Safety Basics</p>
                        <button class="btn btn-primary" onclick="openQuizPage('quiz1')">Open Lesson 1</button>
                    </div>
                    <div class="card topic-card topic-quiz">
                        <h2><span class="topic-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-user-shield"></i></span> Lesson 2</h2>
                        <p>Common Types of Scams</p>
                        <button class="btn btn-primary" onclick="openQuizPage('quiz2')">Open Lesson 2</button>
                    </div>
                    <div class="card topic-card topic-quiz">
                        <h2><span class="topic-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-globe"></i></span> Lesson 3</h2>
                        <p>Internet Safety</p>
                        <button class="btn btn-primary" onclick="openQuizPage('quiz3')">Open Lesson 3</button>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="page-quiz1" class="page-section" hidden>
            <div class="card">
                <button class="btn btn-secondary" onclick="navigateTo('quiz')"><i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Lessons</button>
                <h1><i class="fa-solid fa-shield-halved"></i> Lesson 1: How to Identify a Scam</h1>
                
                <div class="lesson-intro">
                    <h2>💬 Introduction</h2>
                    <p>Scammers try to trick you into giving them money or personal information.</p>
                    <p>They may pretend to be people or organisations you trust, such as your bank, the government, or a delivery company.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>📚 What You Will Learn</h2>
                    <p>After this lesson, you will know how to:</p>
                    <ul class="learning-objectives">
                        <li>Recognise a scam</li>
                        <li>Spot warning signs in messages and phone calls</li>
                        <li>Protect your passwords, PIN and OTP</li>
                        <li>Identify suspicious links and attachments</li>
                        <li>Check whether a message is genuine</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <div class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>📖 Key Concepts</h2>

                    <div class="concept-box">
                        <h3>🏦 Scammers May Pretend to Be Someone You Trust</h3>
                        <p>A scammer may pretend to be:</p>
                        <ul class="concept-list">
                            <li>Your bank</li>
                            <li>The police</li>
                            <li>A government department</li>
                            <li>A delivery company</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p><strong>Important:</strong> They may ask you for personal information.</p>
                        <div class="warning-box">
                            <strong>Remember:</strong> Never give an unexpected caller or message your password, PIN, OTP or banking details.
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="concept-box">
                        <h3>🔐 Keep Your Private Information Private</h3>

Never give your:

Password

PIN

OTP

Banking details

to someone who unexpectedly contacts you.

⏰ Be Careful When Someone Rushes You

Scammers may say:

“Act immediately!”

“Your account will be closed!”

“You must pay now!”

This is a warning sign.

Scammers create urgency to make you act before you have time to think.

🔗 Be Careful With Links

Do not click on a link if you are unsure where it came from.

You should also avoid opening unexpected attachments.

🖼️ Show Me

Add a large picture of a fake scam SMS here.

For example:

🚨 URGENT: Your bank account will be CLOSED today!
Click here immediately to verify your account:
www.example-link.com

Put arrows around:

🔴 URGENT

🔴 The suspicious link

🔴 The request to take immediate action

👀 What should you notice?

The message is trying to rush you.

The link may be unsafe.

You should not click it.

⚠️ Important
Never give someone your:

🔐 Password
🔢 PIN
🔑 OTP
💳 Banking details

If someone asks for these unexpectedly, stop and check first.

📝 Example

You receive this message:

“Your bank account has a problem. Click this link within 10 minutes or your account will be closed.”

What should you do?

❌ Don't click the link.

❌ Don't reply with your banking details.

✅ Contact your bank using its official phone number or website.
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="lesson-section important-reminder">
                    <h2>⚠️ Important Reminders</h2>
                    <div class="reminder-box">
                        <p><strong>Never give someone your:</strong></p>
                        <ul class="sensitive-info">
                            <li><i class="fa-solid fa-lock"></i> Password</li>
                            <li><i class="fa-solid fa-key"></i> PIN</li>
                            <li><i class="fa-solid fa-key"></i> OTP</li>
                            <li><i class="fa-solid fa-credit-card"></i> Banking details</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p><strong>If someone asks for these unexpectedly, stop and check first.</strong></p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="page-quiz2" class="page-section" hidden>
            <div id="quiz-page-quiz2"></div>
        </section>

        <section id="page-quiz3" class="page-section" hidden>
            <div id="quiz-page-quiz3"></div>
        </section>

        <!-- 8. RESOURCES SECTION -->
        <section id="page-resources" class="page-section">
            <div class="card">
                <button class="btn btn-secondary" onclick="navigateTo('safety')"><i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Stay Safe</button>
                <h1>Resources & FAQs</h1>
                <p>Downloadable safety checklists and quick reference guides.</p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 9. DOWNLOADABLE APPS SECTION -->
        <section id="page-apps" class="page-section">
            <div class="card">
                <button class="btn btn-secondary" onclick="navigateTo('skills')"><i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Digital Skills</button>
                <span class="eyebrow"><i class="fa-solid fa-mobile-screen-button"></i> Digital Skills</span>
                <h1><span class="app-icon app-icon-apps app-icon-lg"><i class="fa-solid fa-mobile-screen-button"></i></span> How to Download an App</h1>
                <p>Apps are programs that you can use on your phone. Examples include WhatsApp, Gmail, Facebook, and Google Maps.</p>
                <p>Before you can use an app, you need to download it.</p>

                <p class="visual-guide-heading"><i class="fa-solid fa-eye"></i> Which store does your phone use?</p>
                <div class="icon-callout-grid">
                    <div class="icon-callout">
                        <span class="icon-callout-glyph glyph-apple"><i class="fa-brands fa-apple"></i></span>
                        <p class="icon-callout-label">iPhone</p>
                        <p class="icon-callout-desc">Use the <strong>App Store</strong>. Look for a blue icon with a white "A" shape on your home screen.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="icon-callout">
                        <span class="icon-callout-glyph glyph-playstore"><i class="fa-brands fa-google-play"></i></span>
                        <p class="icon-callout-label">Android phone</p>
                        <p class="icon-callout-desc">Use the <strong>Google Play Store</strong>. Look for a colourful triangle-shaped icon on your home screen.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="step-note step-note-important">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation"></i> <strong>Important:</strong> Only download apps from the official App Store or Google Play Store. Be careful when downloading apps from links in messages or emails.
                </div>

                <ol class="step-list">
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">1</span>
                        <p><strong>Open the app store.</strong> Look at your phone's home screen. Find the App Store if you have an iPhone, or the Google Play Store if you have an Android phone. Tap the icon to open it.</p>
                        <img class="step-image" src="App_icons.jpg" alt="App Store icons" width="300" height="300"> 
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">2</span>
                        <p><strong>Find the Search button.</strong> Look for "Search" — it may look like a magnifying glass <i class="fa-solid fa-magnifying-glass"></i>. Tap Search.</p>
                         <img class="step-image" src="searchbar.png" alt="App Store icons" width="500" height="500">
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">3</span>
                        <p><strong>Search for the app.</strong> A search box will appear. Tap inside it and your keyboard will appear. Type the name of the app you want.</p>
                        <div class="example-box"><span class="example-label">Example</span>If you want WhatsApp, type: <strong>WhatsApp</strong>, then tap Search or press Enter on your keyboard.</div>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">4</span>
                        <p><strong>Choose the correct app.</strong> You will see a list of apps. Check the name and picture of the app carefully before downloading it, then tap the app you want.</p>
                    <div class="example-box"><span class="example-label">Example</span>For WhatsApp, look for the app with the name <strong>WhatsApp Messenger</strong> and a green icon with a white speech bubble and telephone inside. <img class="step-image" src="searching.png" alt="searching" width="300" height="300"></div>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">5</span>
                        <p><strong>Download the app.</strong> The app's information page will open. Look for a button that says "Get", "Install", or has a download icon, and tap it.</p>
                        <img class="step-image" src="intall.png" alt="Download app" width="300" height="300">
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">6</span>
                        <p><strong>Confirm the download.</strong> Your phone may ask you to confirm — you may need to enter your password, use your fingerprint, or use Face ID. Follow the instructions shown on your phone.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">7</span>
                        <p><strong>Wait for the download.</strong> The app will begin downloading; this may take a few moments. When it is finished, you can tap Open to use the app. It will also usually appear on your phone's home screen.</p>
                    </li>
                </ol>

                <div class="step-note">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i> <strong>Need help?</strong> If you are unsure how to download an app, you can return to this page from any of our app instructions.
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 10. WHATSAPP SECTION -->
        <section id="page-whatsapp" class="page-section">
            <div class="card">
                <button class="btn btn-secondary" onclick="navigateTo('skills')"><i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Digital Skills</button>
                <span class="eyebrow"><i class="fa-brands fa-whatsapp"></i> Digital Skills</span>
                <h1><span class="app-icon app-icon-whatsapp app-icon-lg"><i class="fa-brands fa-whatsapp"></i></span> How to Use WhatsApp</h1>
                <p>WhatsApp is an app that uses the internet to let you:</p>
                <img src="whatsapp-icon.png" alt="WhatsApp logo" width="200" height="200">
                <ul class="capability-list">
                    <li><i class="fa-solid fa-message"></i> Send messages</li>
                    <li><i class="fa-solid fa-image"></i> Send photographs</li>
                    <li><i class="fa-solid fa-microphone"></i> Send voice messages</li>
                    <li><i class="fa-solid fa-phone"></i> Make phone calls</li>
                    <li><i class="fa-solid fa-video"></i> Make video calls</li>
                </ul>

                <div class="step-note">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i> <strong>Need help downloading WhatsApp?</strong> If you are unsure how to download an app, refer to our <a href="#apps" onclick="navigateTo('apps')">download instructions</a>.
                </div>
                 <div class="step-note">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-wifi"></i> <strong>Tip:</strong> make sure your phone has an internet connection, and that your camera and microphone are working.
                </div>

                <p class="visual-guide-heading"><i class="fa-solid fa-eye"></i> What to look for on your screen:</p>
                <div class="icon-callout-grid">
                    <div class="icon-callout">
                        <span class="icon-callout-glyph glyph-send"><i class="fa-solid fa-paper-plane"></i></span>
                        <p class="icon-callout-label">Send button</p>
                        <p class="icon-callout-desc">A round green button with a white paper aeroplane. Tap it to send your message.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="icon-callout">
                        <span class="icon-callout-glyph glyph-mic"><i class="fa-solid fa-microphone"></i></span>
                        <p class="icon-callout-label">Microphone button</p>
                        <p class="icon-callout-desc">A small microphone shape inside the text box. Press and hold it to record a voice message.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="icon-callout">
                        <span class="icon-callout-glyph glyph-call"><i class="fa-solid fa-phone"></i></span>
                        <p class="icon-callout-label">Phone call button</p>
                        <p class="icon-callout-desc">A phone-shaped icon at the top of the chat. Tap it to make a voice call.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="icon-callout">
                        <span class="icon-callout-glyph glyph-video"><i class="fa-solid fa-video"></i></span>
                        <p class="icon-callout-label">Video call button</p>
                        <p class="icon-callout-desc">A small video camera icon next to the phone icon. Tap it to make a face-to-face video call.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="icon-callout">
                        <span class="icon-callout-glyph glyph-menu"><i class="fa-solid fa-trash"></i></span>
                        <p class="icon-callout-label">Delete button</p>
                        <p class="icon-callout-desc">A small trash-bin icon. Tap it to delete a voice message before sending it, if you make a mistake.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <h2 class="step-sub-heading">Setting up WhatsApp</h2>
                <ol class="step-list">
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">1</span>
                        <p><strong>Open WhatsApp.</strong> Find the WhatsApp icon on your phone and tap it to open the app.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">2</span>
                        <p><strong>Enter your phone number.</strong> WhatsApp will ask for your mobile phone number. Type it into the box and follow the instructions shown on your screen.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">3</span>
                        <p><strong>Verify your phone number.</strong> WhatsApp may send you a verification code by SMS — a short number used to check that the phone number belongs to you. Type the code into WhatsApp when asked.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">4</span>
                        <p><strong>Open WhatsApp.</strong> After your number has been verified, you will see the WhatsApp home screen. You can now start using WhatsApp.</p>
                    </li>
                </ol>
                <div class="step-note step-note-important">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation"></i> <strong>Important:</strong> Never give your WhatsApp verification code to another person. Someone could use it to try to access your WhatsApp account.
                </div>
                <h2 class="step-sub-heading">How to add a contact</h2>
                <ol class="step-list">
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">1</span>
                        <p><strong>Open WhatsApp.</strong> Find the WhatsApp icon on your phone and tap it to open the app.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">2</span>
                        <p><strong>Find the "New Chat" button.</strong> Look for a small green button with a plus sign. Tap it.</p>
                        <img class="step-image" src="whatapp-contact.jpg" alt="New Chat button" width="300" height="300">
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">3</span>
                        <p><strong>Add a new contact.</strong> Look for "New Contact" or "Add Contact" and tap it.</p>
                        <img class="step-image" src="whataspp-add.jpeg" alt="Add Contact button" width="300" height="300">
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">4</span>
                        <p><strong>Enter the contact's details.</strong> Type the person's name and phone number into the boxes shown on your screen. When you are finished, tap "Save".</p>
                        <img class="step-image" src="whatasapp-addnew.jpeg" alt="Enter contact details" width="300" height="300">
                    </li>
                </ol>

                <h2 class="step-sub-heading">How to send a message</h2>
                <ol class="step-list">
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">1</span>
                        <p><strong>Open Chats.</strong> Open WhatsApp and tap "Chats" at the bottom of the screen.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">2</span>
                        <p><strong>Find the person you want to message.</strong> Look for the Search box, tap it, and type the person's name.</p>
                        <div class="example-box"><span class="example-label">Example</span>If your nurse is saved in your phone as "Nurse Jane", type: <strong>Nurse Jane</strong></div>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">3</span>
                        <p><strong>Choose the person.</strong> Find the correct person in the list and tap their name.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">4</span>
                        <p><strong>Write your message.</strong> A message box will appear at the bottom of the screen. Tap it and type your message.</p>
                        <div class="example-box"><span class="example-label">Example</span>Hello Jane. I will see you tomorrow.</div>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">5</span>
                        <p><strong>Send your message.</strong> Look for the Send button — it may look like a small arrow. Tap it. Your message has now been sent.</p>
                    </li>
                </ol>

                <h2 class="step-sub-heading">How to send a voice message</h2>
                <p>A voice message allows you to speak instead of typing.</p>
                <ol class="step-list">
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">1</span>
                        <p>Open the chat with the person you want to contact.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">2</span>
                        <p>Find the microphone button next to the message box.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">3</span>
                        <p>Press and hold the microphone button, and speak while you continue holding it.</p>
                        <div class="example-box"><span class="example-label">Example</span>"Hello Jane. I just wanted to let you know that I will be home at three o'clock."</div>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">4</span>
                        <p>When you have finished speaking, release the microphone button. Your voice message will be sent.</p>
                    </li>
                </ol>
                <div class="step-note">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-trash"></i> <strong>Tip:</strong> if you make a mistake, look for the delete or trash-bin button shown on the screen, and tap it to delete the recording instead of sending it.
                </div>

                <h2 class="step-sub-heading">How to make a phone call</h2>
                <ol class="step-list">
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">1</span>
                        <p>Open WhatsApp and find the person you want to call.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">2</span>
                        <p>Tap the person's name.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">3</span>
                        <p>Look at the top of the screen and find the phone icon.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">4</span>
                        <p>Tap the phone icon. Your phone call will begin.</p>
                    </li>
                </ol>

                <h2 class="step-sub-heading">How to make a video call</h2>
                <p>A video call allows you to see and speak to the other person.</p>
                <ol class="step-list">
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">1</span>
                        <p>Open the chat with the person you want to call.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">2</span>
                        <p>Look at the top of the screen and find the video camera icon.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">3</span>
                        <p>Tap the video camera icon. The video call will begin.</p>
                    </li>
                </ol>
                <div class="step-note">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-wifi"></i> <strong>Tip:</strong> make sure your phone has an internet connection, and that your camera and microphone are working.
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 11. GMAIL SECTION -->
        <section id="page-gmail" class="page-section">
            <div class="card">
                <button class="btn btn-secondary" onclick="navigateTo('skills')"><i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Digital Skills</button>
                <span class="eyebrow"><i class="fa-solid fa-envelope"></i> Digital Skills</span>
                <h1><span class="app-icon app-icon-gmail app-icon-lg"><i class="fa-solid fa-envelope"></i></span> Gmail</h1>
                <p>Gmail is an email service provided by Google. You can use Gmail to:</p>
                <ul class="capability-list">
                    <li><i class="fa-solid fa-paper-plane"></i> Send messages</li>
                    <li><i class="fa-solid fa-inbox"></i> Receive messages</li>
                    <li><i class="fa-solid fa-image"></i> Send photographs</li>
                    <li><i class="fa-solid fa-file-arrow-up"></i> Send documents</li>
                    <li><i class="fa-solid fa-file-arrow-down"></i> Receive documents</li>
                </ul>
                <p>There are other email services, such as iCloud and Yahoo Mail, but these instructions use Gmail.</p>
                <div class="step-note">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i> <strong>Already have a Gmail account?</strong> You do not need to create another one. Skip ahead to "Writing and sending emails in Gmail" below.
                </div>

                <h2 class="step-sub-heading">How to create a Gmail account</h2>
                <ol class="step-list">
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">1</span>
                        <p><strong>Open your web browser.</strong> For example, Safari on an iPhone, or Google Chrome on many Android phones.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">2</span>
                        <p><strong>Search for Google.</strong> Tap the search bar and type: <strong>Google sign in</strong>, then tap Search.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">3</span>
                        <p><strong>Create your account.</strong> Look for "Create account" and tap it. If Google asks what the account is for, choose "For my personal use".</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">4</span>
                        <p><strong>Enter your name.</strong> Google will ask for your first name and surname.</p>
                        <div class="example-box"><span class="example-label">Example</span>First name: John &nbsp;|&nbsp; Surname: Smith</div>
                        <p>Tap Next.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">5</span>
                        <p><strong>Choose your email address.</strong> Choose an address that is easy for you to remember. A simple option is your first name, a full stop, and your surname.</p>
                        <div class="example-box"><span class="example-label">Example</span>If your name is John Smith, you could choose: <strong>John.Smith@gmail.com</strong></div>
                        <p>Someone else may already have this email address. If that happens, you can add a number, such as your birth year.</p>
                        <div class="example-box"><span class="example-label">Example</span><strong>John.Smith1945@gmail.com</strong></div>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">6</span>
                        <p><strong>Create a password.</strong> Google will show you the rules your password must follow. Choose a password that is difficult for other people to guess, but that you can remember. You may need to type the password twice.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">7</span>
                        <p><strong>Complete the remaining steps.</strong> Google may ask for more information, such as a recovery phone number. Follow the instructions shown on your screen. When you have finished, your Google account and Gmail address will be ready to use.</p>
                    </li>
                </ol>
                <div class="step-note step-note-important">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation"></i> <strong>Important:</strong> Do not use your ID number in your email address, and do not use other sensitive personal information either. This information could give scammers additional information about you.
                </div>
                <div class="step-note step-note-important">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-lock"></i> <strong>Important:</strong> Do not share your password with people you do not trust. Keep your login information somewhere safe.
                </div>

                <h2 class="step-sub-heading">Writing and sending emails in Gmail</h2>
                <div class="step-note">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i> <strong>Need help downloading Gmail?</strong> If you are unsure how to download an app, follow our <a href="#apps" onclick="navigateTo('apps')">download instructions</a>.
                </div>

                <p class="visual-guide-heading"><i class="fa-solid fa-eye"></i> What to look for on your screen:</p>
                <div class="icon-callout-grid">
                    <div class="icon-callout">
                        <span class="icon-callout-glyph glyph-pencil"><i class="fa-solid fa-pencil"></i></span>
                        <p class="icon-callout-label">Compose button</p>
                        <p class="icon-callout-desc">A round button with a pencil, usually in the bottom corner of the screen. Tap it to write a new email.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="icon-callout">
                        <span class="icon-callout-glyph glyph-send"><i class="fa-solid fa-paper-plane"></i></span>
                        <p class="icon-callout-label">Send button</p>
                        <p class="icon-callout-desc">A paper aeroplane icon at the top of your email. Tap it once you are ready to send.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="icon-callout">
                        <span class="icon-callout-glyph glyph-menu"><i class="fa-solid fa-bars"></i></span>
                        <p class="icon-callout-label">Menu button</p>
                        <p class="icon-callout-desc">Three stacked lines at the top of the screen. Tap it to see folders like Sent and Inbox.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <ol class="step-list">
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">1</span>
                        <p><strong>Open Gmail.</strong> Find the Gmail app on your phone and tap it to open Gmail. Sign in using your Gmail address and password if necessary.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">2</span>
                        <p><strong>Start a new email.</strong> Look for the Compose button — it may look like a pencil. Tap it.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">3</span>
                        <p><strong>Choose who will receive the email.</strong> Find the box labelled "To" and type the person's email address.</p>
                        <div class="example-box"><span class="example-label">Example</span>janesmith@gmail.com</div>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">4</span>
                        <p><strong>Add a subject.</strong> The Subject tells the person what your email is about. Keep your subject short.</p>
                        <div class="example-box"><span class="example-label">Example</span>Doctor's appointment</div>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">5</span>
                        <p><strong>Write your message.</strong> Tap the large empty area underneath the subject and type your message.</p>
                        <div class="example-box"><span class="example-label">Example</span>Hello Jane,<br>I would like to confirm my appointment for Tuesday at 10:00.<br>Kind regards,<br>John</div>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">6</span>
                        <p><strong>Send the email.</strong> When you are finished, find the Send button and tap it. Your email will now be sent.</p>
                    </li>
                </ol>
                <div class="step-note">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-wifi"></i> <strong>Tip:</strong> make sure your phone is connected to Wi-Fi or mobile data before sending.
                </div>

                <h2 class="step-sub-heading">How to view emails you have sent</h2>
                <ol class="step-list">
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">1</span>
                        <p>Open Gmail.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">2</span>
                        <p>Tap the menu button — it usually looks like three lines.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">3</span>
                        <p>Tap "Sent". You will now see the emails you have sent.</p>
                    </li>
                </ol>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 12. GOOGLE SEARCH SECTION -->
        <section id="page-googlesearch" class="page-section">
            <div class="card">
                <button class="btn btn-secondary" onclick="navigateTo('skills')"><i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Digital Skills</button>
                <span class="eyebrow"><i class="fa-brands fa-google"></i> Digital Skills</span>
                <h1><span class="app-icon app-icon-google app-icon-lg"><i class="fa-brands fa-google"></i></span> How to Use Google Search</h1>
                <p>Google is a search engine. You can use Google to find:</p>
                <ul class="capability-list">
                    <li><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i> Information</li>
                    <li><i class="fa-solid fa-globe"></i> Websites</li>
                    <li><i class="fa-solid fa-newspaper"></i> News</li>
                    <li><i class="fa-solid fa-store"></i> Shops</li>
                    <li><i class="fa-solid fa-location-dot"></i> Directions</li>
                    <li><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-question"></i> Answers to questions</li>
                </ul>

                <p class="visual-guide-heading"><i class="fa-solid fa-eye"></i> What to look for on your screen:</p>
                <div class="icon-callout-grid">
                    <div class="icon-callout">
                        <span class="icon-callout-glyph glyph-search"><i class="fa-solid fa-magnifying-glass"></i></span>
                        <p class="icon-callout-label">Search box</p>
                        <p class="icon-callout-desc">A long bar near the top of the screen. Tap it to start typing.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <ol class="step-list">
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">1</span>
                        <p><strong>Open Google.</strong> Open the Google app, or your web browser.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">2</span>
                        <p><strong>Find the search box.</strong> Look for the search box and tap inside it.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">3</span>
                        <p><strong>Type what you want to find.</strong> Type a question or words about what you want to find.</p>
                        <div class="example-box"><span class="example-label">Example</span>What time does Checkers close?</div>
                        <p>Then tap Search or press Enter.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">4</span>
                        <p><strong>Look at the results.</strong> Google will show you a list of results. Read them and look for one that seems to answer your question.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">5</span>
                        <p><strong>Open a result.</strong> Tap the website or result that you want to read. The website will open.</p>
                    </li>
                </ol>
                <div class="step-note step-note-important">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation"></i> <strong>Safety tip:</strong> be careful when clicking on unfamiliar websites. Never enter your password, banking information, or ID number into a website unless you are sure that the website is trustworthy.
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 13. FACEBOOK SECTION -->
        <section id="page-facebook" class="page-section">
            <div class="card">
                <button class="btn btn-secondary" onclick="navigateTo('skills')"><i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Digital Skills</button>
                <span class="eyebrow"><i class="fa-brands fa-facebook"></i> Digital Skills</span>
                <h1><span class="app-icon app-icon-facebook app-icon-lg"><i class="fa-brands fa-facebook-f"></i></span> How to Use Facebook</h1>
                <p>Facebook is a social media platform. You can use Facebook to:</p>
                <ul class="capability-list">
                    <li><i class="fa-solid fa-people-group"></i> Keep in contact with family and friends</li>
                    <li><i class="fa-solid fa-message"></i> Send messages</li>
                    <li><i class="fa-solid fa-image"></i> Share photographs</li>
                    <li><i class="fa-solid fa-newspaper"></i> See updates from people you know</li>
                </ul>
                <div class="step-note">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i> <strong>Need help downloading Facebook?</strong> If you are unsure how to download an app, follow our <a href="#apps" onclick="navigateTo('apps')">download instructions</a>.
                </div>

                <h2 class="step-sub-heading">How to create a Facebook account</h2>
                <ol class="step-list">
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">1</span>
                        <p><strong>Open Facebook.</strong> Find the Facebook app on your phone and tap it to open Facebook.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">2</span>
                        <p><strong>Create an account.</strong> If you do not already have a Facebook account, tap "Create New Account". If you already have an account, tap "Log In".</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">3</span>
                        <p><strong>Enter your information.</strong> Facebook will ask for information such as your name, email address or phone number, password, and date of birth. Follow the instructions shown on your screen.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">4</span>
                        <p><strong>Create your account.</strong> When you have entered the required information, tap "Sign Up". Facebook may send a verification code to your phone or email address — follow the instructions to finish creating your account.</p>
                    </li>
                </ol>
                <div class="step-note step-note-important">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation"></i> <strong>Safety tip:</strong> think carefully about the personal information you share on Facebook. Do not publicly share your ID number, banking information, passwords, or other sensitive information.
                </div>

                <h2 class="step-sub-heading">How to find and add friends</h2>

                <p class="visual-guide-heading"><i class="fa-solid fa-eye"></i> What to look for on your screen:</p>
                <div class="icon-callout-grid">
                    <div class="icon-callout">
                        <span class="icon-callout-glyph glyph-search"><i class="fa-solid fa-magnifying-glass"></i></span>
                        <p class="icon-callout-label">Search bar</p>
                        <p class="icon-callout-desc">A long bar at the top of the screen with a magnifying glass. Tap it to search for a person's name.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="icon-callout">
                        <span class="icon-callout-glyph glyph-friend"><i class="fa-solid fa-user-plus"></i></span>
                        <p class="icon-callout-label">Add Friend button</p>
                        <p class="icon-callout-desc">A blue button with a person and a plus sign, next to their profile picture.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <ol class="step-list">
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">1</span>
                        <p><strong>Search for a person.</strong> Find the Search box at the top of the screen, tap it, and type the person's name.</p>
                        <div class="example-box"><span class="example-label">Example</span>Jane Smith</div>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">2</span>
                        <p><strong>Find the correct person.</strong> You may see several people with the same name. Look at their profile picture, name, and other information to help you find the correct person.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">3</span>
                        <p><strong>Send a friend request.</strong> When you find the correct person, tap "Add Friend". The person will receive your friend request, and you will become Facebook friends if they accept it.</p>
                    </li>
                </ol>

                <h2 class="step-sub-heading">How to accept a friend request</h2>
                <ol class="step-list">
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">1</span>
                        <p>Open Facebook.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">2</span>
                        <p>Find the Friends icon.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">3</span>
                        <p>Find the friend request. Check that you know the person, then tap "Confirm" if you know and trust them.</p>
                    </li>
                </ol>
                <div class="step-note step-note-important">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation"></i> <strong>Safety tip:</strong> do not accept friend requests from people you do not know. If you are unsure whether a profile belongs to someone you know, contact that person another way before accepting the request.
                </div>

                <h2 class="step-sub-heading">How to make a Facebook post</h2>
                <ol class="step-list">
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">1</span>
                        <p>Open Facebook.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">2</span>
                        <p>At the top of your home page, look for "What's on your mind?" and tap it.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">3</span>
                        <p><strong>Write your message.</strong> Type what you would like to share. You can also add a photograph if you want to.</p>
                        <div class="example-box"><span class="example-label">Example</span>Had a lovely lunch with my family today!</div>
                    </li>
                    <li class="step-item">
                        <span class="step-number">4</span>
                        <p><strong>Post your message.</strong> When you are ready, tap "Post". Your message will now be shared on Facebook.</p>
                    </li>
                </ol>
                <div class="step-note step-note-important">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation"></i> <strong>Think before you post:</strong> remember that other people may be able to see what you share. Avoid posting private information such as your ID number, passwords, banking information, or home address.
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
        <!-- 13. WORKSHOP SIGN-UP SECTION -->
        <section id="page-signup" class="page-section action-page">
            <div class="action-shell">
                <div class="action-intro action-intro-workshops">
                    <button class="btn btn-quiet" onclick="navigateTo('factcheck')"><i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to workshops</button>
                    <span class="eyebrow"><i class="fa-solid fa-calendar-check"></i> Reserve your place</span>
                    <h1>Learn together. Stay safer online.</h1>
                    <p>Join a friendly, practical workshop designed to make everyday digital tasks feel more manageable.</p>
                    <ul class="action-benefits">
                        <li><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check"></i> Clear, step-by-step guidance</li>
                        <li><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check"></i> Bring your own questions</li>
                        <li><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check"></i> Learn at your own pace</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="action-form-panel">
                    <div class="form-heading">
                        <span class="form-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-pen-to-square"></i></span>
                        <div>
                            <h2>Workshop registration</h2>
                            <p>Tell us where to send the workshop details.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <form id="workshop-signup-form" class="action-form">
                        <div class="field-grid">
                            <div class="field-group">
                                <label for="name">Full name</label>
                                <input type="text" id="name" name="name" placeholder="e.g. Maria Nkosi" required>
                            </div>
                            <div class="field-group">
                                <label for="email">Email address</label>
                                <input type="email" id="email" name="email" placeholder="you@example.com" required>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <!-- OLD AGE HOME DROPDOWN FIELD -->
<div class="form-group">
    <label for="old-age-home" class="form-label">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-house-medical"></i> Select Your Retirement Village / Residence:
    </label>
    <select id="old-age-home" name="oldAgeHome" class="form-select" required>
        <option value="" disabled selected>-- Select an Option --</option>
        <option value="none">Living Independently at Home</option>
        <option value="muckleneuk">Muckleneuk Retirement Village</option>
        <option value="bougainvillea">Bougainvillea Retirement Village</option>
        <option value="silver-villa">Silver Villa Retirement Village</option>
        <option value="sunnyside">Sunnyside Retirement Village</option>
        <option value="other">Other (Not Listed)</option>
    </select>
</div>
                        <div id="workshop-date-group" class="form-group hidden" aria-hidden="true">
                            <label for="workshop-date" class="form-label">
                                <i class="fa-solid fa-calendar-day"></i> Choose a workshop date:
                            </label>
                            <select id="workshop-date" name="workshopDate" class="form-select">
                                <option value="" disabled selected>-- Select a Date --</option>
                                <option value="2026-09-05">Saturday, 5 September 2026</option>
                                <option value="2026-09-12">Saturday, 12 September 2026</option>
                                <option value="2026-09-19">Saturday, 19 September 2026</option>
                            </select>
                        </div>
                        <p class="form-note"><i class="fa-solid fa-lock"></i> Your details are used only to coordinate this workshop.</p>
                        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary btn-submit"><i class="fa-solid fa-paper-plane"></i> Submit registration</button>
                    </form>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
        <!-- 14. CONTACT SECTION -->
        <section id="page-contact" class="page-section action-page">
            <div class="action-shell action-shell-contact">
                <div class="action-intro action-intro-contact">
                    <button class="btn btn-quiet" onclick="navigateTo('factcheck')"><i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to workshops</button>
                    <span class="eyebrow"><i class="fa-solid fa-handshake"></i> Build a partnership</span>
                    <h1>Bring digital confidence to your community.</h1>
                    <p>We would love to hear from retirement villages and community leaders who want to make digital safety more accessible.</p>
                    <div class="contact-callout"><i class="fa-solid fa-comments"></i><span>Share a little about your home and we will get back to you with next steps.</span></div>
                </div>
                <div class="action-form-panel">
                    <div class="form-heading">
                        <span class="form-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-envelope-open-text"></i></span>
                        <div>
                            <h2>Start a conversation</h2>
                            <p>We will use these details to contact you.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <form id="contact-form" class="action-form">
                        <div class="field-grid">
                            <div class="field-group">
                                <label for="contact-name">Full name</label>
                                <input type="text" id="contact-name" name="contact-name" placeholder="e.g. Thabo Mokoena" required>
                            </div>
                            <div class="field-group">
                                <label for="contact-email">Email address</label>
                                <input type="email" id="contact-email" name="contact-email" placeholder="you@example.com" required>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="field-group">
                            <label for="old-age-home-request">Retirement village name</label>
                            <input type="text" id="old-age-home-request" name="old-age-home-request" placeholder="Name of your retirement village" required>
                        </div>
                        <div class="field-group">
                            <label for="contact-message">How can we help? <span>(optional)</span></label>
                            <textarea id="contact-message" name="contact-message" rows="4" placeholder="Tell us about your community or preferred workshop topics."></textarea>
                        </div>
                        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary btn-submit"><i class="fa-solid fa-paper-plane"></i> Send message</button>
                    </form>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

    </main>

    <!-- Site Footer -->
    <footer class="site-footer">
        <div class="container footer-container">
            <span class="footer-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-shield-heart"></i> SilverAssist</span>
            <p class="footer-note">An INL 370 information literacy project, built to help older adults browse, evaluate, and share information online with confidence.</p>
        </div>
    </footer>

    <script>
        function googleTranslateElementInit() {
            new google.translate.TranslateElement({
                pageLanguage: 'en',
                includedLanguages: 'en,af,zu',
                autoDisplay: false
            }, 'google_translate_element');
        }
    </script>
    <script src="https://translate.google.com/translate_a/element.js?cb=googleTranslateElementInit"></script>
    <!-- Link to your local JavaScript file -->
    <script src="script.js"></script>
</body>
</html>